# .trivyignore — documented, ID-scoped suppressions for the Trivy scan
# (.github/workflows/trivy.yml) and its GitHub Advanced Security check.
#
# Policy: this file lists ONLY specific advisory / misconfig IDs that have
# been reviewed and accepted. It is NOT a blanket ignore — any NEW finding
# (new CVE, new package, new misconfig rule) still surfaces and fails the
# check, forcing a fresh review. Mirror of npm-wasm/audit-ci.jsonc for the
# npm-audit gate. Accepted on PR #26.
#
# REVIEW BY: 2026-09-28
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) npm dependency CVEs rooted in the pinned agentic-flow@2.0.12-fix.8
#    runtime tree (npm-wasm) plus the AIMDS/ and root sample lockfiles.
#    Cleanly-fixable advisories are already floored to patched, same-major
#    versions via npm-wasm/package.json "overrides". The CVEs below have no
#    non-breaking fix (npm's only remedy is a semver-major agentic-flow
#    downgrade that would regress the QUIC runtime, untestable in CI).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
